         <gmd:abstract>
            <gco:CharacterString>The Australian Water Outlook website (http://awo.bom.gov.au/) underpins a suite of services and national outputs produced by the Bureau of Meteorology including:&#xD;
&#xD;
·       Historical: daily gridded outputs of precipitation, soil moisture, evapotranspiration (potential and actual), runoff and deep drainage from 1911 until yesterday. A range of other evapotranspiration products are also provided. Updated daily. Temporal aggregations: ‘Month-to-date', ‘monthly’ and ‘annual’ temporal aggregations&#xD;
·       Seasonal forecasts (1-3 month) with monthly outputs available for root-zone soil moisture, evapotranspiration and runoff – updated monthly.&#xD;
·       Projections of changes in precipitation, soil moisture, evapotranspiration and runoff for a series of aggregated periods out to the end of the century.&#xD;
&#xD;
The Historical data collection: Various historical modelled outputs are available through the Australian Water Outlook including:&#xD;
·       Historical water balance information: precipitation and modelled soil moisture, evapotranspiration (potential and actual), runoff and deep drainage from 1911 until yesterday. The Bureau's hydrological model AWRA-L v7.0 was used to generate the outputs, based on historical climate forcing also generated by the Bureau.&#xD;
&#xD;
·       Historical evapotranspiration: estimates covering 1975 until yesterday for products that require wind input (synthetic pan evaporation, open water, short crop, tall crop) and Morton's areal potential evapotranspiration.&#xD;
&#xD;
For more about the AWO services, including links to relevant technical reports and journal articles, please see the About page (https://awo.bom.gov.au/about/overview/forecasts) on the AWO website.</gco:CharacterString>
         </gmd:abstract>
